  "worked_solution": "We know that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(tan\u2061x)={sec}^{2}\u2061x.$ Applying these formulas, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\sqrt{x}+3tan\u2061x) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(tan\u2061x) \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}})+3({sec}^{2}\u2061x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}+3{sec}^{2}\u2061x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
